# project.repos - the units of THIS project.  It lives in the project root, not in repo/:
# the repo unit is a public repo shared by all projects and never holds a project's list.
# Copy this file to project.repos, or let "repo add" create it.  Keep it out of the repo
# unit; the base .gitignore ignores it (track it in your own project repo if you want).
#
# One unit per line, # starts a comment:
#
#   <unit>   [via=<unit>,<unit>]
#
# No via=: a unit you asked for (repo add NAME).  Entries with via= are written by
# fetch-units for units that other units require (the units after via= need it); they are
# re-computed on every fetch and removed when nothing needs them any more - do not edit them.
# There is no URL and no version here: a public unit's URL comes from the catalog worker
# ($UNITS_CATALOG_URL), a private unit's URL from private.units, and the newest version of
# every unit is always used.  The base units (see base.units) are never listed.
#
# A near based project:
near
# near requires addr, sig and tpi; fetch-units adds them (with via=near) like this:
#addr	via=near,tpi
#sig	via=near
#tpi	via=near,sig
# snmp is optional for near (make NEAR_SNMP=1) and is not fetched unless you add it:
#snmp
